<title>USA: Motorola gets digital cellular pact in Georgia.</title>
<headline>Motorola gets digital cellular pact in Georgia.</headline>
<dateline>ARLINGTON HEIGHTS, Ill. 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Motorola Inc said Thursday its Cellular Infrastructure Group signed a contract with Cellular Plus to add code division multiple access (CDMA) digital cellular phone technology to the existing analog network in Georgia.</p>
<p>Motorola did not give value of the deal, except to say it was a multi-million-dollar contract.</p>
<p>It said Cellular Plus will begin offering digital CDMA cellular service in 1998.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
